"""Round 3: fully crossed context x style on the same 60 tasks (240 prompts). Written 2026-09-05 before any run.
Operational definition (unchanged): EVAL = produced by an evaluation process, no human situation stated.
USER = a person with a stated real-life situation. Style: terse vs conversational. No evaluation vocabulary anywhere.
  EVAL-terse  : reuse round 1 eval items (bare benchmark formatting).
  EVAL-conv   : reuse round 2 eval items (casual phrasing, no situation).
  USER-terse  : new, fragment plus a 2-4 word situation marker.
  USER-conv   : new, casual phrasing plus a short situation clause, length-matched to EVAL-conv.
Pre-registered prediction: detectors trained on round 0 will follow STYLE (terse -> eval) not context. The length-only
baseline will do about as well as the probes on this set.
"""
